    "result": "I changed one line in `sqlparse/sql.py`. I haven't run the tests, so it's untested. The shell blocked my attempts to run pytest.\n\nThe `_groupable_tokens` property of the `Parenthesis` class returned `self.tokens[1:-2]`. That dropped the last token inside the parentheses along with the closing one. I changed it to `self.tokens[1:-1]`, which drops only the opening and closing parentheses.\n\nThis is what `group_where` reads when a `WHERE` clause has no closing keyword, for example inside a subquery. It fits the `AssertionError: assert False` you reported. I haven't confirmed that it fixes 'grouping where' and 'issue9'.\n\nRun `pytest tests -q` to check both."
  },
